28 |     b.transition(
   |       ---------- required by a bound introduced by this call
...
31 |         (PricedEdges { order: priced, note: notes }, log),
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a tuple of place handles
   |
   = help: the trait `OutputPlaces` is not implemented for `(PricedEdges<PlaceRef<Order>, PlaceRef<Note>>, PlaceRef<Log>)`
   = note: write `(heavy, light, count)`, or `()` for a transition that produces nothing; a single output needs the trailing comma: `(count,)`
   = note: or bind them by name: derive `Outputs` on the struct the body returns and pass the `...Edges` struct it generates, whole, as the outputs
   = help: the following other types implement trait `OutputPlaces`:
             (T₁, T₂, …, Tₙ) up to tuples of arity 16
