error[E0277]: a transition body must return its outputs, or a `Result` of them
  --> tests/ui/fail_outputs_in_tuple.rs:32:9
   |
28 |     b.transition(
   |       ---------- required by a bound introduced by this call
...
32 |         |order: Order| (Priced { order, note: None }, Log(String::from("priced"))),
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `(Priced, Log)` is not a transition outcome
   |
   = help: the trait `IntoOutcome<(PricedEdges<PlaceRef<Order>, PlaceRef<Note>>, PlaceRef<Log>), _>` is not implemented for `(Priced, Log)`
   = note: positional: outputs `(PricedEdges<PlaceRef<Order>, PlaceRef<Note>>, PlaceRef<Log>)` want a tuple of that many slots, where slot i is `T`, `Option<T>` or `Vec<T>` for the type of output place i, and `()` for no outputs at all
   = note: named: the struct whose `#[derive(Outputs)]` generated the outputs' `...Edges` struct, each field going to the output of the same name
   = note: routed: a value that is not a tuple, whose every payload goes to the output place that holds its type. Derive `Routed` on the enum or struct you return
   = note: distribution: a `Distribution` of (place, token) pairs, built with `Distribution::new().to(place, token)`, for choosing between output places of the same type
   = note: any of these may be wrapped in `Result<_, E>` where `E: std::error::Error + Send + Sync + 'static`; a `Result` always means failure, never routing
help: the following other types implement trait `IntoOutcome<Outputs, Marker>`
  --> src/body.rs
   |
   | / impl<Outputs, O, E, M> IntoOutcome<Outputs, marker::Failing<M>> for Result<O, E>
   | | where
   | |     O: IntoOutcome<Outputs, M>,
   | |     E: Error + Send + Sync + 'static,
   | |_____________________________________^ `Result<O, E>` implements `IntoOutcome<Outputs, Failing<M>>`
   |
